# Numerical Policy Parsing

The numerical policy uses **fixed-width floating-point parsing** via `strconv.ParseFloat`.

**Exact parsing code:**
```go
cv, err := strconv.ParseFloat(version, 64)
if err != nil {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("failed to parse invalid numeric value '%s'", version)
}
```

This approach converts version strings to 64-bit floating-point numbers, not arbitrary-precision arithmetic. Consequently, it has inherent precision limitations for very large numbers compared to using `big.Float`.

